  "comment": "kiln.ui's game-UI integration on the client (enshrouded.exe 26404966). Evidence: docs/re/game-ui.md. The game's UI is immediate mode: GameUiSystem calls its update fn (GameUiFrame, registered at app start) once per UI frame on the UI thread; the frame context sits in the global UiApp only while that call runs. GameUiFrame's first argument is the GameUiSystem+0x10; its +sys.data is the persistent GameUiData (first field: the GameUi state, whose byte +state.ui_state is keen::UiState and +state.play the play data, whose byte +play.hud_screen is keen::HudScreenType and +play.interaction the entity the player interacts with). Menu entries are drawn by two entry renderers: MainMenuEntry(state, {text, len, fnv64, 8 option bytes}) in the main menu builder and SystemMenuEntry({text, len, fnv64}, 1, attention) in the system (pause) menu and a few other lists; both return true on activation and take part in the frame's focus/gamepad navigation. kiln.ui draws its entries through them right before the Settings entry (main menu: both layout branches, ShroudForge 1.7.6's insertion point; system menu: the Settings entry), identified by the call's return address. CraftingMenu is the crafting menu builder (every frame while one is open); its last selected recipe id is stored at data+data.craft_recipe (the player's own menu) or *(data+data.station_recipe) (a station). Main-menu page (feature ui.menu_page, docs/re/game-ui.md \"Main-menu pages\", client 26430625, static analysis): the PreGame state block (never cached: the UI's state store frees blocks not touched in a frame) keeps the current page at +pregame.page; PreGameGoTo(pregame, page) only compares and writes it. MainMenuEntry's first argument is pregame+pregame.main_menu at the Settings and Credits call sites. Kiln's MODS entry calls PreGameGoTo(pregame, pregame.page_credits); its hook on PreGameCredits (bool(void)) answers only the call from the PreGame page switch (return address PreGameCreditsRet): true stays, false makes the game go back to page_main_menu itself. The UI system's update writes the canvas (sys.canvas_w/h, UI units), the viewport (sys.viewport: x, y, w, h floats, pixels) and pixels per unit (sys.px_per_unit) at system offsets; GameUiFrame's first argument is system+sys.frame_arg. The error popup shows while the byte at frame_arg-relative sys.popups + popups.error is set. ui.menu_page_sound: UiPlaySound(*UiApp, &copy of cfg+cfg.sound_entry_cancel) as PlaySelection's back does.",
